stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Resolving

    Resolving --> Resolved: Lookup finishes first
    Resolving --> TimedOut: Hop deadline fires first
    Resolving --> CancelledAtOnce: Turn cancel arrives (Design B walks away)

    Resolving --> WaitingSelectCancel: Turn cancel arrives (Design A)
    WaitingSelectCancel --> CancelledAfterSignal: Signal interrupts lookup
    WaitingSelectCancel --> StuckOnLookup: Lookup ignores signals (breaks CancelIsPrompt)

    Resolving --> IgnoringCancel: Turn cancel arrives (Current ignores flag)
    IgnoringCancel --> StuckOnLookup: Lookup stays blocked (breaks CancelIsPrompt)

    CancelledAtOnce --> CallerFreed: Caller returns and frees arena
    CallerFreed --> LateLookupCleaned: Late lookup finishes into its own job and frees it (Design B)

    Resolved --> [*]
    TimedOut --> [*]
    CancelledAfterSignal --> [*]
    LateLookupCleaned --> [*]
    StuckOnLookup --> [*]

    note right of StuckOnLookup
        Shortest broken path (current.cfg, 3 steps):
        Resolving -> IgnoringCancel -> StuckOnLookup
        Shortest broken path (design-a.cfg with signal-ignoring lookup, 4 steps):
        Resolving -> WaitingSelectCancel -> StuckOnLookup
        Both violate CancelIsPrompt.
    end note

    note right of LateLookupCleaned
        Design B passes CancelIsPrompt, NoUseAfterReturn, and DeadlineStillWorks
        even when getaddrinfo retries EINTR or ignores signals and finishes late.
        Omitted: mutant-* configurations (b-caller-frees-early, b-non-atomic,
        b-reads-caller-flag, b-no-deadline, a-no-check) and Ideal simulation.
    end note
